0..74 Comment "// A flow at a universe above the smallest: the codes it relates are large"
75..152 Comment "// types, which pack a type in a field, so they live one level up and so does"
153..225 Comment "// the flow between them. The classifier `Flow(Type[+, 1], A, B)` is the"
226..294 Comment "// directed hom of that universe (Gratzer, Weinberger and Buchholtz,"
295..355 Comment "// _Directed univalence in simplicial homotopy type theory_,"
356..429 Comment "// arXiv:2407.09146, Definition 1.2), stated at its level as `Path` is at"
430..507 Comment "// every level; the kernel replays each declaration here at its flow over the"
508..538 Comment "// level-one universe (#1628)."
540..618 Comment "/// A list of values of a type it carries: a large type, since a field holds a"
